  FLOP/B = 9 means the step is pure memory traffic.  A ridge point of
  ~295 FLOP/B (H100) / ~201 (A100) means anything under that is
  bandwidth-limited, so the whole game is not touching DRAM.
  'inf' = the step costs zero extra traffic only IF it is fused into
  its neighbour; materialised it would be [B,NT,HV,C,V] = 128 MB.

