--- what fusing across the scan boundary is worth ---
v_new [B,NT,HV,C,V] spilled (write+read)      256.0 MB
  intensity, fused across the scan (base)       37.5 FLOP/B
  intensity, v_new spilled to DRAM               34.0 FLOP/B
  absolute floor: read q,k,v,g + write o        640.0 MB  ->  143.9 FLOP/B
  so even a PERFECTLY fused KDA is still 2.1x below the H100 ridge point (295).
  The gate + cumsum alone (steps 0,1) are 1280 MB = 52% of the traffic and 0 of the FLOPs.

--- the traps (what a naive tensorised port would materialise) ---
h, per-chunk states [B,NT,HV,K,V]      256.0 MB   (0.27 GB)  <- only avoidable by fusing the scan
full score matrix  [B,H,T,T]           4096.0 MB   (4.29 GB)  <- softmax-attention shape; KDA must NOT do this
  per head: 32.0 MB, i.e. O(T^2).  A compiler that fuses the
  chunk loop into one graph never has to build it -- but it also
  cannot parallelise the loop, which is the actual difficulty.

